A||||11||hugh||Holiday time-Happy or sad?||||1||
Z||000000||hugh||12-25-2000||02:05 PM||||I started thinking about how lucky I am while watching 4 of my grandchildren unwrapping their presents and It hit me like a bolt of lightning.There are so many people young and old that don't have happy holidays for a variety of reasons.Loneliness,poverty,sickness(themselves,a friend or a relative)It doesn't seem fair that someone in this world should be unhappy when there is so much that could be done to help them.I don't know how to remedy that kind of problem,except the few usual ways,like food drops at the stores.If the forum members put away $1 a week to use for someones else's benefit during the course of the year it could be considered the premium paid on a peace of mind insurance policy that may make any holiday a happier one.A phone call to someone you think may be lonesome to let them know you are thinking of them can help alleviate depression.A case of pet food to your local shelter can do wonders for you.Visit someone in a hospital or rest home,even for a few minutes,and you will recharge your satisfaction battery.I'm sorry to have rambled on for so long,but I almost feel guilty for being so lucky.     ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||12-25-2000||03:22 PM||||I was thinking the exact same thing yesterday. Not about how to rememdy it persay, but just about how so many people must feel horrible on Christmas (homeless, etc). At least in this small of a city (100,000), I'm hoping that the majority are having a good time. I don't particularly enjoy this day as my favourite day of the year, but I know I could be a h*ll of a lot worse off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BENGAL4||12-25-2000||03:50 PM||||This christmas has been very rough on me and my family. For those of you who dont know, my wife passed away unexpectedly in July. This has been very hard and very sad. She is missed by so many people. My kids are hanging in there and we are going to make it. The one good thing that has happened this Christmas, is that it has gotten me closer to the real reason we celebrate. So here I am publicly stating, Thank you God for the gift of your Son. I thank you for our health and blessings. And finally when I start feeling sorry for myself, help me see others that have it alot worse than I do.<P>MERRY CHRISTMAS and spend time with your loved ones, you never know if it is the last time.<P>PEACE.<P>86GT 3800 II S/C ||||reg||9
Z||000003||hugh||12-25-2000||06:52 PM||||Bill,I hope every day is brighter than the day before for you and your kids,God Bless.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-25-2000||10:15 PM||||Happy or sad?...Mixed.  Ask me in a few weeks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||12-26-2000||01:35 PM||||Mine sucked.  My wife is moving out next week.  She's the one that want's to split, but I'm supposed to act all happy on Christmas like nothing is wrong.  Screw it!||||reg||8
Z||000006||deceler8||12-26-2000||02:20 PM||||Have to agree...generally sad.<P>Weather's bad, markets are bad...economic uncertainty...fighting in the Middle East...<P>I just want to feel the warm sun on my face again. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||12-26-2000||03:45 PM||||i tend to stay a little down so holidays are kind of non events for me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Spyro86SE||12-27-2000||12:58 PM||||bahumbug  holidays suck never liked chrismas and probaly never will <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spryologo_1_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||12-27-2000||02:34 PM||||For all of you who have lost loved ones or are going through family upheaveals or other misfortunes, my heart goes out to you. I will keep you in my prayers. <BR>As for the "Christmas Holiday", I think it has gotten way too commercialized. I kind of dread all the stress and crowds. Of course, I can remember folks saying that as far back as I can remember. <BR>As for my own Christmas...? Could have been better. Could have been MUCH worse. Spent last Thursday and Friday night in the hospital. Haven't been that frightened in a long time. Just thanking God that I'm here. <P>I wish peace and happiness to you all.<P>Steve    <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||hugh||12-27-2000||08:44 PM||||I'm sorry to hear that members of this Fiero family aren't as happy as they could be.From reading your posts on other subjects,I must admit I'm surprised the posts on this thread have the tone they do. I'll ask this question next year(I hope) and maybe your year will be a great one and your response will show it.I start off every day reading the cartoons in the paper,when you start your day laughing it has to be a good one.  I'm not a religious person,but I do believe in God,may he bless you all.||||reg||14
Z||000011||fiero56||12-27-2000||10:31 PM||||A girl I met today had a terrible holiday. Her sister was in a bad car accident last week, both legs are broken, her kidneys are both bad, one lung is bad, her back is broken, and her family doesn't know if they should keep her on the respirator or not.<BR>Her brother has an illness, and on Christmas day, was told he has 3-4 weeks left to live. <P>Made me think how well I have it, and how different the holidays are for everyone. <P>I have a friend who just totalled his car in a 3 car accident yesterday. He is fine, but is without a car for now.||||reg||1
